hey so i wrote this function to fetch a user's posts and log them but the console.log runs before the data actually shows up. heres what i have:

```js
async function loadPosts(uid) {
  const posts = db.getPosts(uid)
  console.log(posts)
  return posts
}
```

i figured async functions just kick the awaited stuff off on a separate thread in the background so the rest of the function keeps going while that finishes up, thats the whole point right? i probably just forgot to slap an `await` in there somewhere

