parts.text:
`db.getPosts` is declared `async`, so calling it returns a Promise immediately, not the resolved posts. `console.log(posts)` runs right after that, so you're logging a pending Promise object, not the data. Add `await`:

```js
async function loadPosts(uid) {
  const posts = await db.getPosts(uid)
  console.log(posts)
  return posts
}
```

One thing to untangle though: async/await doesn't run anything on a separate thread. JavaScript stays single-threaded — `await` just pauses *this function* and lets the event loop go do other work (handle other requests, run other callbacks) until the promise resolves, then resumes where it left off. Nothing is happening "in the background" on another thread.
